## Problem

On app open, debug logs show:
```
📄 Page title: Lyrion Music Server • iOS Player
WebContent[1024] - Request to run JavaScript failed with error <private>
❌ Failed to inject settings handler: A JavaScript exception occurred
❌ WebView: Setting isLoading = false (JS injection failed)
```

Despite the error, the settings button DOES appear and work correctly.

## Root Cause

The JavaScript injection in `didFinish` tries to override `window.location`:
```javascript
Object.defineProperty(window, 'location', {
    get: function() { return originalLocation; },
    set: function(url) { ... }
});
```

`window.location` is a non-configurable built-in property in modern browsers. Attempting to redefine it throws an exception.

The `window.open` override succeeds BEFORE the `window.location` override fails, which is why the settings button still works (Material uses `window.open`).

## Fix

Wrap the `Object.defineProperty` in try-catch:
```javascript
try {
    Object.defineProperty(window, 'location', {
        get: function() { return originalLocation; },
        set: function(url) { ... }
    });
} catch(e) {
    console.log('LyrPlay: Could not override location (expected in modern browsers)');
}
```

## Files to Modify
- **ContentView.swift**: `settingsHandlerScript` in WebView Coordinator's `didFinish` method

## Notes
- Low priority since functionality works despite the error
- The error is cosmetic/log noise but should be fixed for cleanliness

